2026-09-27T09:44:39.6437341Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6437753Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6438838Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6440075Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6440184Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6440662Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6441045Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6441484Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6441611Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6441892Z ================
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6442046Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6442259Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6442744Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6443033Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6443187Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6443556Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6443796Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6443982Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6444504Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6444984Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6445957Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6446679Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6446825Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6447424Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6448140Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6448529Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6448950Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6449516Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6449631Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6536703Z ========
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6536918Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6538950Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6540982Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6541304Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6541944Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6543091Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6543883Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6544615Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6545194Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6545776Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6545914Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6546239Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6546435Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6547886Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6549445Z 
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6550599Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6551798Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:44:39.6552094Z 
